       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 RC mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max dose)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you intend, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I can then enter it as written. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
